# Mock Vacancy Dataset

The project ships with a pre-built dataset at **`vacancies.json`** (project root). Do not generate new mock vacancies — load this file directly in ingestion scripts and tests.

## Vacancy Schema

Every record complies with the following fields:

| Field | Type | Notes |
|-------|------|-------|
| `role` | string | IT/engineering roles only |
| `description_of_vacancy` | string | Full text: stack, requirements, responsibilities |
| `salary` | integer \| null | Monthly rate in USD/EUR; `null` if unspecified |
| `company` | string | Hiring company name |
| `contacts` | string | Email, Telegram handle, or other contact endpoint |
| `status_of_role` | list[string] | Subset of: `"Full-time"`, `"Part-time"`, `"Project"`, `"Remote"`, `"Hybrid"` |

## Embedded Validation Fault Cases

The dataset intentionally includes records that simulate critical error states to stress-test validation, routing, and embedding pipelines. These records are distributed throughout the file:

| # | Fault Type | What is broken |
|---|-----------|----------------|
| 1 | **Out-of-Domain Role** | `role` is a non-engineering position (e.g., marketing) |
| 2 | **Missing Mandatory Key** | `role` field is absent entirely |
| 3 | **Type Mismatch** | `status_of_role` is a plain string instead of a list |
| 4 | **Empty Description** | `description_of_vacancy` is `""` |
| 5 | **Null Payload Metadata** | `status_of_role` is `null` |
| 6 | **Empty Contacts** | `contacts` is `""` |

When writing ingestion or validation tests, cover all 6 fault types using records already present in `vacancies.json` — do not create separate fixture files for these cases.
